WEBVTT

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:08.751
Baby, carry on

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:13.723
When the winds of tomorrow howl

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:19.762
Keep on laughing, be the cocky
person that you are

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:22.915
No matter what happens

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:34.298
Storming through life, during the
day you feel invincible

00:00:36.136 --> 00:00:41.939
Of course, there are those nights
when everything falls apart

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:48.871
You find yourself humming
an old melody

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:56.065
Through the pain you feel as sweat
stings your wounded knee

00:00:56.089 --> 00:00:58.100
Baby, carry on

00:00:58.124 --> 00:01:02.527
Even on those mornings when
the wind blows in your face

00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:09.211
Keep on laughing, and even the moon
shall one day look upon you

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:11.213
Someday your journey will come

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:16.452
| can at least make one
miracle happen

00:01:16.476 --> 00:01:19.221
Until that day

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:25.150
Don't you surrender! Angel Blue!

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:44.547
What a nice, lazy day!

00:01:44.571 --> 00:01:49.441
| can't wait to get to the next
town so we can eat.

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:57.059
You've got the mind-set of a
schoolboy, one in the lower grades.

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:59.261
Did you say something, motor head?

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:01.686
You can't hear either? Too bad.

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:08.671
Hey, Ritsuko! Get us into town!

00:02:08.695 --> 00:02:10.406
Oh, shut up!

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:12.108
Just a bit farther.

00:02:12.132 --> 00:02:15.432
Come on, just a little more. Please?

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:19.996
You can do it.

00:02:25.245 --> 00:02:27.373
A little more! A little more!

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:48.599
You did your best. Rest a while.

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:53.816
Out of gas again! And in the
middle of nowhere too!

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:57.286
This thing gets the world's
worst gas mileage.

00:02:57.310 --> 00:03:00.189
Look at this huge crack!

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:01.423
Here!

00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:01.690
What?
Here!

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:02.424
What?

00:03:02.448 --> 00:03:02.925
What? Don't act dumb! Squeeze
one of those gasoline fruits!

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:05.418
Don't act dumb! Squeeze one
of those gasoline fruits!

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:11.167
Here! That's the last of it.

00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:15.150
The Junpei gasoline refinery is now
closed. Squeeze all you want.

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:17.907
There's no point in staying here.

00:03:17.931 --> 00:03:21.443
We'll leave the tank for now
and go into town.

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:23.445
We need to do some shopping anyway.

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:24.937
No way!

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:27.950
Why leave it behind just for now

00:03:27.974 --> 00:03:30.500
when we could abandon it forever?

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:34.043
You mean throw away the T-747

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:50.428
Listen to me, Junpeil!

00:03:50.964 --> 00:03:53.008
You went too far back there!

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:55.644
You made her so angry!

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:58.228
Try to understand what that girl
might be going through!

00:03:59.505 --> 00:04:02.202
| wonder what caused the damage
to all of these buildings?

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:04.653
Looks like we got enough food.

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:05.854
Yes.

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:06.155
Listen to me!
Yes.

00:04:06.179 --> 00:04:07.289
Listen to me!

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:07.356
Listen to me! | can hear you too well.
We looked for a gasoline fruit, didn't we?

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:11.647
| can hear you too well. We looked
for a gasoline fruit, didn't we?

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:15.397
Just because this world has
a fruit that produces gas,

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:18.701
doesn't mean you can always
find one, right?

00:04:18.725 --> 00:04:21.490
It's a wonder we got this far
in that bucket of bolts.

00:04:22.195 --> 00:04:29.111
Sometimes the best thing to do
is cut your losses.

00:04:29.135 --> 00:04:36.085
| wonder how this world came to have
a gasoline-producing fruit?

00:04:36.109 --> 00:04:39.170
Animals! I say we go with
animals this time!

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:41.924
| say we find a strong horse! Yeah!

00:04:41.948 --> 00:04:45.661
Who cares what it is as
long as it's big?

00:04:45.685 --> 00:04:49.965
A cow? A mule? As long as it
can replace a tank!

00:04:49.989 --> 00:04:52.034
I've had my fill of useless pets

00:04:52.058 --> 00:04:54.336
that are only good at gobbling
up the groceries.

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:56.438
Who are you calling a pet, jackass?

00:04:56.462 --> 00:04:58.540
The screaming dog that's sitting
on my arm, that's who.

00:04:58.564 --> 00:05:01.844
Which mouth did that come from?

00:05:01.868 --> 00:05:03.545
Which mouth is saying all of those
terrible things about his friends?

00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:06.248
Get your paws off of me! Which mouth is saying
all of those terrible things about his friends?

00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:06.982
Which mouth is saying all of those
terrible things about his friends?

00:05:07.006 --> 00:05:10.185
Is it this one? Is it this mouth?

00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:11.768
It's a bear.

00:05:12.712 --> 00:05:16.205
A bear would be terrific as
long as it couldn't talk.

00:05:21.654 --> 00:05:23.465
What a jerk!

00:05:23.489 --> 00:05:26.151
| can squeeze out gasoline
just as well as he does!

00:05:30.196 --> 00:05:31.686
Come on!

00:05:32.932 --> 00:05:35.367
| can do it!

00:05:44.644 --> 00:05:50.708
I didn't know it was this hard to
get gasoline for the T-74.

00:06:05.231 --> 00:06:09.429
A teddy bear? Why?

00:06:10.803 --> 00:06:12.848
That's it!

00:06:12.872 --> 00:06:16.151
The bear can replace the tank!

00:06:16.175 --> 00:06:18.821
Junpei, please calm down.

00:06:18.845 --> 00:06:20.313
Meow!

00:06:20.947 --> 00:06:24.259
Wait! A bear doesn't say meow!

00:06:24.283 --> 00:06:27.344
I don't think that's the pressing
issue right now!

00:06:28.421 --> 00:06:31.700
If it can carry all of us, who cares
whether it meows or chirps?

00:06:31.724 --> 00:06:33.168
Junpei!

00:06:33.192 --> 00:06:34.103
There it is!

00:06:34.127 --> 00:06:34.670
It's the Cat Spirit!
There it is!

00:06:34.694 --> 00:06:36.059
It's the Cat Spirit!

00:06:37.397 --> 00:06:39.074
A teddy bear this time?

00:06:39.098 --> 00:06:41.276
That bastard won't get away this time!

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:44.580
We're just passing though.
What is going on in this town?

00:06:44.604 --> 00:06:46.315
This is a spirit.

00:06:46.339 --> 00:06:47.282
A spirit?

00:06:47.306 --> 00:06:47.816
That's right. It's a cat spirit that
possesses stuffed animals, A spirit?

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:51.553
That's right. It's a cat spirit that
possesses stuffed animals,

00:06:51.577 --> 00:06:53.978
and then tears apart our village.

00:07:01.254 --> 00:07:03.198
Look, it's sharpening its claws.

00:07:03.222 --> 00:07:05.816
No! That's my house!

00:07:10.730 --> 00:07:12.494
Now I get it.

00:07:13.166 --> 00:07:14.843
This is terrific.

00:07:14.867 --> 00:07:18.881
How much do you want for
the cat-bear-spirit-thing?

00:07:18.905 --> 00:07:20.416
What?!

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:21.917
You're out of your mind!

00:07:21.941 --> 00:07:25.220
Do you know how much destruction
that thing has caused?

00:07:25.244 --> 00:07:26.922
The beast must die!

00:07:26.946 --> 00:07:29.711
That's right! We will kill it!

00:07:31.451 --> 00:07:33.852
Open your eyes!

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:39.935
Look at it with fresh eyes!

00:07:39.959 --> 00:07:41.737
Is it acting out of malice?

00:07:41.761 --> 00:07:43.705
Do you see a killer instinct at work?

00:07:43.729 --> 00:07:45.697
Or is it just trying to have fun?

00:07:47.733 --> 00:07:51.613
How did you all become so heartless?

00:07:51.637 --> 00:07:53.749
A cat just wants to play.

00:07:53.773 --> 00:07:56.242
So what if it playfully knocks
over a few houses?

00:07:57.176 --> 00:07:58.644
Oh, Junpei.

00:08:01.547 --> 00:08:03.325
No need to thank me.

00:08:03.349 --> 00:08:07.718
Just come along on our journey
and carry us on your back.

00:08:17.296 --> 00:08:18.764
Junpei!

00:08:26.806 --> 00:08:29.184
Damn you, bear-cat-thing!

00:08:29.208 --> 00:08:30.886
Kill it! Kill it! Kill it!

00:08:30.910 --> 00:08:32.378
Junpei...

00:08:38.985 --> 00:08:41.249
Who did it? Who shot the arrow?

00:08:42.088 --> 00:08:44.166
I'm sorry. It scared me so badly.

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:46.068
Idiot!

00:08:46.092 --> 00:08:48.871
If it was that easy to kill, we would
have done it long ago.

00:08:48.895 --> 00:08:51.907
So what? Once it burns up, it won't
bother you anymore, right?

00:08:51.931 --> 00:08:54.776
No, it means the spirit is free to roam.

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:57.546
It will search for another stuffed
animal to inhabit.

00:08:57.570 --> 00:09:00.267
Locking it up in a sturdy metal chest
seems to be the only answer.

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:05.173
Hold on! That damn thing is
catching my house on fire!

00:09:07.713 --> 00:09:11.126
Too bad. I thought it would make the
perfect replacement for that tank.

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:14.643
| guess a useful animal
is hard to come by.

00:09:18.925 --> 00:09:22.384
Are we going to say good-bye
on a bridge like this one?

00:09:23.863 --> 00:09:26.341
You were such a wonderful tank,

00:09:26.365 --> 00:09:28.595
considering that you weren't built
to travel long distances.

00:09:32.038 --> 00:09:35.008
| guess we will no longer be able
to rampage together.

00:09:53.159 --> 00:09:55.753
Is this really goodbye?

00:09:56.596 --> 00:09:58.155
| won't do it!

00:09:58.764 --> 00:10:01.665
| can't throw you away, T-74!

00:10:03.569 --> 00:10:06.038
We've been through tougher
situations together!

00:10:07.506 --> 00:10:11.374
Together all along... all along...

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:32.994
A stuffed dog that meows?

00:10:37.903 --> 00:10:40.668
This world sure has its share
of strange things in it.

00:10:42.241 --> 00:10:46.735
You're soaked. Did somebody
throw you away, little guy?

00:10:48.681 --> 00:10:51.548
Yes, I understand.

00:10:53.619 --> 00:10:56.198
A spirit that possesses stuffed animals.
Who would believe it?

00:10:56.222 --> 00:10:59.034
It's certainly earned quite a
reputation around here.

00:10:59.058 --> 00:11:00.902
It's Public Enemy Number One
in this town,

00:11:00.926 --> 00:11:03.905
so I don't think we should
be involved with it.

00:11:03.929 --> 00:11:06.308
For once, you may have a point.

00:11:06.332 --> 00:11:08.061
Ms. Airi!

00:11:08.834 --> 00:11:09.911
Ritsuko?

00:11:09.935 --> 00:11:10.312
Darn! She's back to her old
behavior already. Ritsuko?

00:11:10.336 --> 00:11:12.614
Darn! She's back to her old
behavior already.

00:11:12.638 --> 00:11:14.402
Look at this! Just look!

00:11:15.508 --> 00:11:18.967
Look, I found a living stuffed dog!

00:11:19.945 --> 00:11:21.413
Look at it!

00:11:27.286 --> 00:11:30.499
Isn't she adorable? I just
can't put her down.

00:11:30.523 --> 00:11:33.068
I've named her already.

00:11:33.092 --> 00:11:34.856
Her name is Mike.

00:11:39.565 --> 00:11:41.932
What? What's the matter
with you guys?

00:11:48.908 --> 00:11:50.185
It vanished!

00:11:50.209 --> 00:11:50.385
Maybe we finally ran it out of town.
It vanished!

00:11:50.409 --> 00:11:52.454
Maybe we finally ran it out of town.

00:11:52.478 --> 00:11:54.389
That's probably what happened.

00:11:54.413 --> 00:11:56.780
That is not what happened.

00:12:02.354 --> 00:12:04.099
The Master Monk!

00:12:04.123 --> 00:12:08.151
That thing still stalks this town.

00:12:08.794 --> 00:12:12.741
We cannot afford to have this
trouble spread any further.

00:12:12.765 --> 00:12:15.410
We must end it ourselves.

00:12:15.434 --> 00:12:16.902
Understood?

00:12:19.071 --> 00:12:21.216
And that's what happened.

00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:24.820
| see. Who could imagine
such a thing?

00:12:24.844 --> 00:12:26.321
| understand.

00:12:26.345 --> 00:12:29.324
Wow, for once you're not making
a big fight out of it.

00:12:29.348 --> 00:12:31.407
| won't let anyone harm Mike!

00:12:33.018 --> 00:12:36.631
You're not listening! Not listening
to one word we've said!

00:12:36.655 --> 00:12:40.102
You should see how angry
those villagers are!

00:12:40.126 --> 00:12:42.504
Then we'll take her without telling
them we have her with us.

00:12:42.528 --> 00:12:45.987
No! We don't have room for
any more extra baggage!

00:12:46.932 --> 00:12:49.629
Besides, we already have a pet dog.

00:12:51.036 --> 00:12:52.714
Who are you calling a pet?

00:12:52.738 --> 00:12:55.016
I'm minding my own business, and
you start in with the insults!

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:56.818
When have you ever minded
your own business?!

00:12:56.842 --> 00:12:58.420
Something about you drives me nuts!

00:12:58.444 --> 00:13:01.923
Don't be so selfish... so selfish.

00:13:01.947 --> 00:13:03.915
Stop being so selfish!

00:13:04.583 --> 00:13:06.745
You guys are so terribly selfish.

00:13:07.453 --> 00:13:10.465
You want to abandon the T-74
because it runs out of gas!

00:13:10.489 --> 00:13:12.934
You speak of Mike as being a
disposable piece of baggage!

00:13:12.958 --> 00:13:15.723
| have nothing... nothing...

00:13:17.329 --> 00:13:25.329
| have nothing in this world that
| can get rid of so easily.

00:13:25.671 --> 00:13:27.332
Ritsuko...

00:13:31.076 --> 00:13:32.771
We find you at last!

00:13:38.417 --> 00:13:40.784
You want a piece of us, old man?

00:13:44.023 --> 00:13:47.084
Young lady, please hand over
the little stuffed dog.

00:13:47.760 --> 00:13:55.477
We cannot allow that spirit to wreak
havoc on our lives. Please.

00:13:55.501 --> 00:13:59.181
No! Mike would never act out
of malice towards anyone!

00:13:59.205 --> 00:14:02.869
It has nothing to do with the
intentions of its heart.

00:14:03.976 --> 00:14:06.421
As good citizens, it is our duty

00:14:06.445 --> 00:14:09.758
to maintain the order and
safety of our town.

00:14:09.782 --> 00:14:12.561
Are my words unjust?

00:14:12.585 --> 00:14:14.296
No...

00:14:14.320 --> 00:14:16.531
You are very compassionate.

00:14:16.555 --> 00:14:18.400
But have compassion for
those whose lives

00:14:18.424 --> 00:14:20.722
have been damaged by this
terrible spirit as well.

00:14:24.830 --> 00:14:27.663
Finally! The spirit is in our hands!

00:14:28.534 --> 00:14:29.544
Oh, yeah!

00:14:29.568 --> 00:14:30.512
Thank goodness!
Oh, yeah!

00:14:30.536 --> 00:14:31.046
Thank goodness!
We've got you now!

00:14:31.070 --> 00:14:32.333
We've got you now!

00:14:33.906 --> 00:14:35.374
Mike!

00:14:35.975 --> 00:14:38.239
Thank you for making a hard decision.

00:14:38.777 --> 00:14:39.988
All of you.

00:14:40.012 --> 00:14:40.255
Nothing says thank you better
than a nice, fat reward. All of you.

00:14:40.279 --> 00:14:43.291
Nothing says thank you better
than a nice, fat reward.

00:14:43.315 --> 00:14:45.443
How about a big, roomy animal?

00:14:46.952 --> 00:14:49.764
Now we just need to find
a sturdy metal chest

00:14:49.788 --> 00:14:51.499
and seal this thing inside.

00:14:51.523 --> 00:14:55.619
Yes. Hey, what about this big
metal box right here!

00:14:56.295 --> 00:14:59.374
We could break the bridge and
send it into the river!

00:14:59.398 --> 00:15:02.959
Good idea! Hey, is this your box?

00:15:18.517 --> 00:15:20.395
Ritsuko!

00:15:20.419 --> 00:15:22.197
It's all for the best.

00:15:22.221 --> 00:15:26.501
| guess this is the last service that
the T-74 will ever perform.

00:15:26.525 --> 00:15:28.503
What an ego you have!

00:15:28.527 --> 00:15:31.606
Everything's okay with you now
that you have a horse!

00:15:31.630 --> 00:15:37.512
It's only fair for them to pay us for
letting them dump the T-74.

00:15:37.536 --> 00:15:39.004
Right?

00:15:39.772 --> 00:15:42.317
You and your one track mind!

00:15:42.341 --> 00:15:45.420
Four people cannot fit on this thing.

00:15:45.444 --> 00:15:47.422
How in the world are we
going to get around?

00:15:47.446 --> 00:15:50.848
Then you can walk! Every dog needs
a good walk each day!

00:15:51.784 --> 00:15:55.277
We haven't finished discussing this yet!

00:15:57.222 --> 00:15:58.600
All set!

00:15:58.624 --> 00:15:58.700
Let's seal the bastard inside!
All set!

00:15:58.724 --> 00:16:00.669
Let's seal the bastard inside!

00:16:00.693 --> 00:16:03.571
Should we put it in the big
part or the small part?

00:16:03.595 --> 00:16:07.054
The small part will do!
It goes in there!

00:16:12.104 --> 00:16:12.881
Mike!

00:16:12.905 --> 00:16:13.581
Ritsuko, don't do anything!
Mike!

00:16:13.605 --> 00:16:16.597
Ritsuko, don't do anything!

00:16:17.843 --> 00:16:20.107
Let's knock the bridge down!

00:16:23.649 --> 00:16:25.427
Mike will die in there!

00:16:25.451 --> 00:16:30.082
Knock it off! It's a stuffed toy!
It's not a living being!

00:16:40.466 --> 00:16:41.934
<i>Here we go!</i>

00:16:43.335 --> 00:16:44.803
Wrong!

00:16:49.975 --> 00:16:52.808
You're wrong! It is a living thing!

00:16:53.579 --> 00:16:54.556
Ritsuko!

00:16:54.580 --> 00:16:55.056
You idiot!
Ritsuko!

00:16:55.080 --> 00:16:56.291
You idiot!

00:16:56.315 --> 00:16:57.192
Hey!

00:16:57.216 --> 00:16:57.792
Stop!
Hey!

00:16:57.816 --> 00:16:58.681
Stop!

00:16:59.284 --> 00:17:00.752
It's dangerous!

00:17:08.527 --> 00:17:09.504
Oh, my gosh.

00:17:09.528 --> 00:17:10.005
You stupid fool!
Oh, my gosh.

00:17:10.029 --> 00:17:11.463
You stupid fool!

00:17:18.504 --> 00:17:19.972
Ritsuko!

00:17:33.919 --> 00:17:35.387
Ritsuko!

00:17:46.965 --> 00:17:49.711
Hey! Did you find the girl?

00:17:49.735 --> 00:17:52.547
Of course not! We can't do it alone!

00:17:52.571 --> 00:17:56.618
Rocks have settled on the hatches!

00:17:56.642 --> 00:17:59.202
She will be trapped inside!

00:17:59.878 --> 00:18:04.526
Gather all of the rope and oxen you
can! Act fast or she'll die!

00:18:04.550 --> 00:18:06.494
Understood! Hurry, men!

00:18:06.518 --> 00:18:07.328
Yes, Sir!

00:18:07.352 --> 00:18:07.996
Wait!
Yes, Sir!

00:18:08.020 --> 00:18:08.816
Wait!

00:18:09.922 --> 00:18:13.501
The spirits of the wind
have informed me

00:18:13.525 --> 00:18:15.203
that there are no signs of life

00:18:15.227 --> 00:18:17.992
coming from inside the tank!

00:18:22.367 --> 00:18:26.770
Ritsuko!

00:19:10.315 --> 00:19:11.783
Ritsuko!

00:19:16.021 --> 00:19:18.066
It's a miracle!

00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:19.854
<i>Hit</i>

00:19:20.792 --> 00:19:23.591
| guess we survived!

00:19:24.429 --> 00:19:26.454
Yes, we did, Mike! We made it!

00:19:28.700 --> 00:19:30.278
Mike!

00:19:30.302 --> 00:19:31.779
Mike!

00:19:31.803 --> 00:19:35.865
Mike! What's wrong with you? Mike!

00:19:37.876 --> 00:19:39.344
Mike...

00:19:48.220 --> 00:19:52.179
Mike saved Ritsuko. I wonder
where her spirit went?

00:19:52.724 --> 00:19:57.338
She sacrificed her last strength
just so she could...

00:19:57.362 --> 00:19:59.574
Oh, I can't bear it!

00:19:59.598 --> 00:20:01.376
| can't either.

00:20:01.400 --> 00:20:03.845
The horse got scared off
by the commotion

00:20:03.869 --> 00:20:06.167
and now all we have is
that lousy tank.

00:20:07.506 --> 00:20:09.284
Hey, Ritsuko!

00:20:09.308 --> 00:20:11.786
More fuel for your scrap heap!

00:20:11.810 --> 00:20:13.922
This can't get us anywhere.

00:20:13.946 --> 00:20:16.958
We go as far as we can go together.

00:20:16.982 --> 00:20:19.928
That came with us from Japan too.

00:20:19.952 --> 00:20:21.596
You moron.

00:20:21.620 --> 00:20:23.998
Junpei is as low on brains
as we are on gas,

00:20:24.022 --> 00:20:26.320
but he still has some
redeeming features.

00:20:27.693 --> 00:20:30.071
Mike may have moved the rocks,

00:20:30.095 --> 00:20:32.473
but how did the T-74 drive out?

00:20:32.497 --> 00:20:34.309
It was completely out of gas.

00:20:34.333 --> 00:20:35.343
Out of gas?!

00:20:35.367 --> 00:20:35.810
Out of gas?
Out of gas?!

00:20:35.834 --> 00:20:37.245
Out of gas?

00:20:37.269 --> 00:20:40.315
Yeah, how could it...

00:20:40.339 --> 00:20:42.671
Unless there was some
gas left in the tank.

00:20:43.375 --> 00:20:45.935
Ritsuko, were you lying to us?!

00:20:50.082 --> 00:20:51.826
Oh, for heaven's sake!

00:20:51.850 --> 00:20:54.820
Look what you're doing! You're
wasting all that precious fuel!

00:21:04.930 --> 00:21:05.940
Impossible.

00:21:05.964 --> 00:21:06.407
Maybe not.
Impossible.

00:21:06.431 --> 00:21:07.421
Maybe not.

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:09.468
Mike?

00:21:10.435 --> 00:21:14.048
| guess we don't have to worry
about gasoline anymore.

00:21:14.072 --> 00:21:15.250
| guess not.

00:21:15.274 --> 00:21:15.550
Let's get going while there's
still some sunlight. | guess not.

00:21:15.574 --> 00:21:18.586
Let's get going while there's
still some sunlight.

00:21:18.610 --> 00:21:20.942
Ritsuko? Mike? Is that okay with you?

00:21:21.480 --> 00:21:22.948
Yes!

00:21:27.919 --> 00:21:30.183
Mike, welcome home!

00:21:53.578 --> 00:22:00.662
It's okay to take a break on a day
when you feel despondent

00:22:00.686 --> 00:22:07.635
Life is long and fickle, you know

00:22:07.659 --> 00:22:14.709
| can make you a hundred
times stronger

00:22:14.733 --> 00:22:17.979
Come on, let's sleep for now

00:22:18.003 --> 00:22:21.883
Hold me gently

00:22:21.907 --> 00:22:26.868
Even if you met a dinosaur

00:22:28.980 --> 00:22:35.663
You are the kind of person that
would just laugh it off

00:22:35.687 --> 00:22:42.370
Winning through flower gardens
and storm ravaged plains

00:22:42.394 --> 00:22:50.011
| can hear how the times are
changing around us

00:22:50.035 --> 00:22:56.684
Distinguishing both the
sour and the sweet

00:22:56.708 --> 00:23:04.708
Just don't give up, because the genius
always comes at the end

00:23:10.589 --> 00:23:14.548
What's this? A love letter
in my foot locker?

00:23:15.394 --> 00:23:19.240
| already have someone I long for.

00:23:19.264 --> 00:23:20.742
Let's see here.

00:23:20.766 --> 00:23:22.810
"This is a chain letter of pain."

00:23:22.834 --> 00:23:24.779
Damn! Bastard!

00:23:24.803 --> 00:23:27.181
| have enough pain coming to
me in the next episode!

00:23:27.205 --> 00:23:30.251
Episode six is about a mysterious
book that has just been found.

00:23:30.275 --> 00:23:32.687
Next Those Who Hunt Elves:

00:23:32.711 --> 00:23:35.289
"The Horrors of the Most Horrible
Spell of All Time"!

00:23:35.313 --> 00:23:37.577
Keep your eyes open for it!
